  "releaseNotes": "An ordering finds where an element whose key moves it more than a few places belongs, and where a new element belongs, by descending the order once, where it searched the order by halves and found each element it compared by its position; moving an element to a random place takes 0.65x the time among a thousand elements and 0.62x among ten thousand, moving it 32 places 0.77x and 512 places 0.68x, and adding and removing an element 0.94x, allocating the same.",
